#
# Copies whose source offset is not aligned to the destination's subtrees: the
# copied tree is the canonical tree (repr.bend `build`) of the source words from
# the offset, `bq`, which waits on a free tree `T` of the statement so that the
# checker never unfolds it at a closed size.

